## Why This Is Asked

Tests real-world composition of runtime modules, per-tenant isolation, and advanced hooks patterns.

## Key Concepts

- React.lazy and Suspense for on-demand modules
- useSyncExternalStore to subscribe to external per-tenant data
- Memoized selectors keyed by tenantId/moduleId
- Runtime Module Registry pattern
- Safe unmount and cleanup on tenant switches

## Code Example

```javascript
// Pseudo-code: Module registry and host wiring
import React, { createContext, useContext, Suspense, lazy } from 'react'

export const ModuleRegistryContext = createContext({ register: () => {} })

export function ModuleHost({ tenantId }) {
  const { getModuleLoader } = useContext(ModuleRegistryContext)
  const modules = ['ModuleA', 'ModuleB']
  return (
    <div>
      {modules.map((id) => {
        const Loader = lazy(getModuleLoader(id))
        return (
          <Suspense key={id} fallback={<div>Loading {id}...</div>}>
            <Loader tenantId={tenantId} />
          </Suspense>
        )
      })}
    </div>
  )
}
```

